{
 "name": "southeast_farallon_island",
 "description": "Southeast Farallon Island (California) side-on from the sea: bare jagged grey-brown granite with white guano streaks, crack strokes, a rocky boulder shoreline and Lighthouse Hill, a steep cone on the left third (peak about (-244,-185)) with a tiny white lighthouse on top. Flat marine-terrace ledge on the right half: top at y -148 from x 40 to 380 (put elephant_seal_pup anchors on y -148). No trees, no buildings. Taller and jagged, unlike the long flat seal_island. Anchor bottom-centre on the waterline; x -500..500, y -220..+4 .",
